ld him captive.",["role"]="The imprisoned scout could pick the courtyard door’s rusty lock before returning to Hadrec with his report."},["id"]="catalog-unit-3849",["kind"]="figure",["newSubject"]=false,["qualification"]="CLASSIC_HISTORICAL_CONTEXT_NOT_CURRENT_FOREVER_MECHANICS_OR_PERSONAL_EXPERIENCE",["related"]={"shadowfang-keep"},["sourceKey"]="wiki-adamant",["sourceURL"]="https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Deathstalker_Adamant",["sourceVersion"]="instance-boss-histories-2026-10-26-r3",["title"]="Deathstalker Adamant"},{["aliases"]={"Deathstalker Vincent"},["fieldEvidence"]={["context"]={["method"]="PUBLIC_INDEXED_SECONDARY_EXCERPT",["receiptID"]="wiki-vincent",["receiptSHA256"]="b8b57e4188d2efb5b9f963b07254e808ec5c64aa9131faa77adf5d174b2784cc"},["history"]={["method"]="PUBLIC_INDEXED_SECONDARY_EXCERPT",["receiptID"]="wiki-vincent",["receiptSHA256"]="b8b57e4188d2efb5b9f963b07254e808ec5c64aa9131faa77adf5d174b2784cc"}},["fields"]={["context"]="Arugal’s monologue threatened to make Vincent’s remains an example of what awaited trespassers.",["history"]="Vincent vanished with Adamant during the reconnaissance ordered before an assault on Shadowfang. His companion was imprisoned, while Vincent lay slain within the keep."},["id"]="catalog-unit-4444",["kind"]="figure",["newSubject"]=false,["qualification"]="CLASSIC_HISTORICAL_CONTEXT_NOT_CURRENT_FOREVER_MECHANICS_OR_PERSONAL_EXPERIENCE",["related"]={"shadowfang-keep"},["sourceKey"]="wiki-vincent",["sourceURL"]="https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Deathstalker_Vincent",["sourceVersion"]="instance-boss-histories-2026-10-26-r3",["title"]="Deathstalker Vincent"},{["aliases"]={"Baron Silverlaine"},["fieldEvidence"]={["history"]={["method"]="PUBLIC_INDEXED_SECONDARY_EXCERPT",["receiptID"]="wiki-shadowfang-history",["receiptSHA256"]="9fac4d32e456223ee78f6d23736ae7f9459adeb94d8344fe045a08c65c4fd5ab"}},["fields"]={["history"]="The baron’s keep fell to the worgen Arugal had summoned. His vengeful ghost haunted the stronghold that had been his home."},["id"]="catalog-unit-3887",["kind"]="creature",["newSubject"]=false,["qualification"]="CLASSIC_HISTORICAL_CONTEXT_NOT_CURRENT_FOREVER_MECHANICS_OR_PERSONAL_EXPERIENCE",["related"]={"shadowfang-keep"},["sourceKey"]="wiki-shadowfang-history",["sourceURL"]="https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/SFK",["sourceVersion"]="instance-boss-histories-2026-10-26-r3",["title"]="Baron Silverlaine"},{["aliases"]={"Shadowfang Keep"},["fieldEvidence"]={["history"]={["method"]="PUBLIC_INDEXED_SECONDARY_EXCERPT",["receiptID"]="wiki-shadowfang-history",["receiptSHA256"]="9fac4d32e456223ee78f6d23736ae7f9459adeb94d8344fe045a08c65c4fd5ab"},["location"]={["method"]="PUBLIC_INDEXED_SECONDARY_EXCERPT",["receiptID"]="wiki-shadowfang-history",["receiptSHA256"]="9fac4d32e456223ee78f6d23736ae7f9459adeb94d8344fe045a08c65c4fd5ab"}},["fields"]={["history"]="Arugal’s desperate summons fought the Scourge but turned against the wizards as well. Guilt drove him to adopt the worgen as children and retreat into the fallen baron’s keep.",["location"]="The keep rose above Pyrewood’s small hamlet in Silverpine Forest."},["id"]="shadowfang-keep",["kind"]="instance",["newSubject"]=false,["qualification"]="CLASSIC_HISTORICAL_CONTEXT_NOT_CURRENT_FOREVER_MECHANICS_OR_PERSONAL_EXPERIENCE",["related"]={},["sourceKey"]="wiki-shadowfang-history",["sourceURL"]="https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/SFK",["sourceVersion"]="instance-boss-histories-2026-10-26-r3",["title"]="Shadowfang Keep"},{["aliases"]={"Grubbis"},["fieldEvidence"]={["appearance"]={["method"]="PUBLIC_INDEXED_SECONDARY_EXCERPT",["receiptID"]="wiki-grubbis",["receiptSHA256"]="8528e8d5514262360a91d9afc2af4b87661426efe8755958d9f40b52dd848c50"},["context"]={["method"]="PUBLIC_INDEXED_SECONDARY_EXCERPT",["receiptID"]="wiki-grubbis",["receiptSHA256"]="8528e8d5514262360a91d9afc2af4b87661426efe8755958d9f40b52dd848c50"},["relationships"]={["method"]="PUBLIC_INDEXED_SECONDARY_EXCERPT",["receiptID"]="wiki-grubbis",["receiptSHA256"]="8528e8d5514262360a91d9afc2af4b87661426efe8755958d9f40b52dd848c50"}},["fields"]={["appearance"]="The contaminated city’s gas had caused this trogg to grow to an extraordinary size.",["context"]="The original dungeon confrontation brought Grubbis and Chomper into the struggle near the end of Emi Shortfuse’s demolition work.",["relationships"]="His basilisk Chomper accompanied him through Gnomeregan’s tunnels."},["id"]="catalog-unit-7361",["kind"]="creature",["newSubject"]=false,["qualification"]="CLASSIC_HISTORICAL_CONTEXT_NOT_CURRENT_FOREVER_MECHANICS_OR_PERSONAL_EXPERIENCE",["related"]={"gnomeregan"},["sourceKey"]="wiki-grubbis",["sourceURL"]="https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Grubbis",["sourceVersion"]="instance-boss-histories-2026-10-26-r3",["title"]="Grubbis"},{["aliases"]={"Electrocutioner 6000"},["fieldEvidence"]={["appearance"]={["method"]="PUBLIC_INDEXED_SECONDARY_EXCERPT",["receiptID"]="wiki-electrocutioner",["receiptSHA256"]="e91cefb2ff066a89247fc68ac30226721bd807968d7d1d2d0265c417aa07acba"},["location"]={["method"]="PUBLIC_INDEXED_SECONDARY_EXCERPT",["receiptID"]="wiki-electrocutioner",["receiptSHA256"]="e91cefb2ff066a89247fc68ac30226721bd807968d7d1d2d0265c417aa07acba"},["relationships"]={["method"]="PUBLIC_INDEXED_SECONDARY_EXCERPT",["receiptID"]="wiki-electrocutioner",["receiptSHA256"]="e91cefb2ff066a89247fc68ac30226721bd807968d7d1d2d0265c417aa07acba"}},["fields"]={["appearance"]="The Electrocutioner was a spider-shaped mechano-tank built to wield electricity.",["location"]="The tank occupied the upper central platform of Gnomeregan’s Launch Bay.",["relationships"]="Lieutenant Tom Crankle, nicknamed Sizzlepants, piloted it among Thermaplugg’s leper-gnome followers."},["id"]="catalog-unit-6235",["kind"]="creature",["newSubject"]=false,["qualification"]="CLASSIC_HISTORICAL_CONTEXT_NOT_CURRENT_FOREVER_MECHANICS_OR_PERSONAL_EXPERIENCE",["related"]={"gnomeregan"},["sourceKey"]="wiki-electrocutioner",["sourceURL"]="https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Electrocutioner_6000",["sourceVersion"]="instance-boss-h